  - state/candidateStore.test.ts, +60/-1;
  - tools/recordCandidate.ts, +11;
  - tools/recordCandidate.test.ts, +17.

Scope: verify and review the landed bytes. Do NOT re-implement, revert or re-land working code. Change a file only for a defect QA requires, and keep this row at 400 net or less. Measure with `git show --numstat --format= dc13b0e -- <the 5 paths>`.

Out of scope:
- the delivery predicate and consumers (CQ-V01);
- execution identities on check runs (CQ-V02);
- runner authentication (CQ-V03);
- client or wrapper changes.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test

implementationPlan.description:
Prove DoD 1-4 on HEAD with focused tests and mutation probes.
- Work in an isolated Linux snapshot of HEAD: native Linux node_modules symlinked (memory gotcha-linux-vitest-reuse-native-node-modules) and every MOE_* variable unset (memory gotcha-seat-env-leaks-into-daemon-tests). Never run vitest in /mnt/d.
- Run `npx vitest run src/state/candidateStore.test.ts src/tools/recordCandidate.test.ts src/delivery/acceptance.test.ts`. The acceptance file is held-out: read it, never edit it.
- Map each DoD item to its landed test in the protectedEntries section of candidateStore.test.ts:
  - DoD1: 'persists a valid protectedEntries list and hands out copies of it', including [];
  - DoD2: the badEntries table (INVALID_INPUT naming the entry, nothing written, the 2001-entry bound included);
  - DoD3: 'treats protectedEntries as frozen', covering undefined vs [] vs changed lists, the identical replay, unchanged bytes, and deep copies via the copy-mutation assertions;
  - DoD4: recordCandidate.test.ts 'declares protectedEntries as a closed {path, oid} list and records it', plus the held-out acceptance record_candidate case, which still passes with no protectedEntries.
- Run six mutation probes on a scratch copy of the HEAD bytes, never the shared tree. Each must fail a named test:
  (i) drop the strictly-ascending/duplicate check: the 'unsorted entries' and 'duplicate path' rows;
  (ii) make BLOB_OID_RE case-insensitive: the 'an uppercase oid' row;
  (iii) compare `stored.protectedEntries ?? []` with `incoming ?? []`: the frozen test;
  (iv) make `copy` shallow: the copy-mutation assertion;
  (v) raise MAX_PROTECTED_ENTRIES to 2001: the '2001 entries' row;
  (vi) remove protectedEntries from record_candidate's inputSchema: the tool test.
- Record each result in the step note. If a probe SURVIVES, that is a DoD test gap. Add the one minimal assertion that kills it, inside the 5 files, and note it.
